# Invariant ignores shared across every project in this monorepo - OS/editor churn and generic
# build-tool caches that look the same regardless of which project produced them. Project-specific
# output paths (APK layout, wails' build/bin, this app's own data/archive dirs, etc.) stay in that
# project's own .gitignore instead (git applies both automatically within one repo - no config
# needed) - only move a pattern here if it would apply unchanged in any project of that general
# kind (any JVM project, any project touched on a Mac, etc.).

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editors / IDEs
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Java / Gradle (Android today, any future JVM tooling)
.gradle/
*.class

# Android build output (any Android project, regardless of module layout)
*.apk
*.ap_
*.dex

# Native build caches (Android NDK / CMake)
.cxx/
.externalNativeBuild/

# Node/npm-based frontend tooling
node_modules/

# Generic
*.log

# Claude Code session-local state (not project source)
.claude/*.lock

# Privately-installed dev tools (see `make install-tools` / the ROOT/LOCAL_BIN comment in
# Makefile) - machine/checkout-specific, never source.
/.local/

# go.work / go.work.sum are NOT ignored here (unusually for a Go project) - `make generate`
# depends on them: crossing from controller/'s module into tools/dbstore's to run its generator
# fails outright ("directory ... outside main module or its selected dependencies") without a
# workspace tying the two together. See docs/quirks/dev-tooling-windows.md.

# Code-generation stamps (see `make generate` / tools/go-deps) - local build state, not source.
**/*.gen.json.stamp

# controller's runtime state (SQLite DB, single-instance lock, downloaded clip archive - see
# controller/.gitignore) lands here instead of under controller/ if the binary is ever launched
# with the repo root as its working directory (e.g. `make run-controller`, which launches from
# wherever `make` itself runs) - controller/internal/appdirs resolves these relative to launch
# cwd, not a fixed app-data path. See docs/implementation/HANDOFF-implementation.md.
/data/
/archive/
